CD32 read-ahead regression
=========================

Build with test-devices-cd-readahead or test-devices-cd-readahead-quick.
The native Amiga CD component test group selects this test.

Generate a disposable data disc on the host:

    python3 make_disc.py /tmp/cd-readahead.iso

Mount it as CD unit 0 and run devices/cd/cdreadahead. Use a stock PAL CD32
with 2 MiB Chip RAM. The test selects 150 sectors/second and alternates
between distant two-sector reads, checking the exact data and surrounding
buffer guards. Between reads it leaves the read-ahead stream running and
issues the change-number/change-state queries used by filesystems.

Each generated data sector contains its sector number and inverse, followed
by a predictable byte pattern. No commercial game or ROM is required to
construct the disc. An unrelated disc will fail the data checks.

Success: 32 reads, 0 failures, exit status 0.
